        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">How to Optimize Your Resume for ATS</h2>

        <p>Most large companies use Applicant Tracking Systems to filter resumes before a human recruiter ever sees them. These systems scan for relevant keywords, proper formatting, and structured content. If your resume doesn't meet their criteria, it gets filtered out — regardless of your qualifications.</p>

        <p>Online Resume ATS helps you understand how these systems work and what you can do to pass them. Our tools are completely free, run entirely in your browser, and never store your data on any server.</p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">What Makes a Resume ATS-Compatible?</h3>

        <p>An ATS-friendly resume follows a few core principles: use standard section headers like "Experience," "Education," and "Skills." Avoid tables, multi-column layouts, images, and headers/footers — these confuse most parsing engines. Save your resume as a clean PDF (not a scanned image), and always include keywords that match the job description you're applying to.</p>

        <p>Our ATS Score Checker compares your resume directly against a job description. It identifies which keywords you're missing, flags formatting problems, and gives you a clear score with specific suggestions to improve.</p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Tools Built for Every Stage of Your Job Search</h3>

        <p>The <a href="/ats-score-checker" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">ATS Score Checker</a> gives you an instant compatibility score when you paste your resume alongside a job posting. The <a href="/resume-keywords" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">Keyword Analyzer</a> breaks down your resume into hard skills, soft skills, and action verbs, highlighting gaps you might not notice on your own.</p>

        <p>Need to pivot industries? The <a href="/domain-converter" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">Domain Converter</a> maps generic resume language to industry-specific terminology across eight sectors including fintech, healthcare, cybersecurity, and AI/ML. And when you're ready to apply, the <a href="/cover-letter-generator" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">Cover Letter Generator</a> creates tailored letters from your resume content using five different professional templates.</p>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-4">Privacy-First Approach</h3>

        <p>Unlike most resume tools that upload your documents to their servers, everything here processes locally in your browser. Your resume never leaves your device, never gets stored in a database, and never gets used to train AI models. We built it this way because your career documents contain sensitive information that deserves protection.</p>

        <p>There's no account to create, no trial to expire, and no premium tier hiding the features you actually need. Use every tool as many times as you want, for free.</p>
